# Force LF line endings for files that run inside Linux containers,
# regardless of the local machine's core.autocrlf setting. Without this,
# a Windows checkout (core.autocrlf=true, the Git-for-Windows default)
# silently converts these to CRLF, which corrupts shebang lines
# (#!/bin/bash\r is not a valid interpreter path) and breaks the file
# the moment it's baked into a Docker image and executed on Linux --
# exact symptom: "No such file or directory" even though the file
# demonstrably exists and is chmod +x.
*.sh text eol=lf
Dockerfile text eol=lf
*.yml text eol=lf
*.yaml text eol=lf
